::ALG2_U03_L02_Q16::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_Q16
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
What is the range of the parent cube root function?
{
~A. y >\= 0#This incorrectly restricts the outputs. The parent cube root function has no upper or lower endpoint, so its range is all real numbers.
~B. x >\= 0#This incorrectly restricts the outputs. The parent cube root function has no upper or lower endpoint, so its range is all real numbers.
~C. y <\= 0#This incorrectly restricts the outputs. The parent cube root function has no upper or lower endpoint, so its range is all real numbers.
=D. all real numbers#Correct. Cube root outputs include negative, zero, and positive values.
}


::ALG2_U03_L02_Q17::
Question ID: ALG2_U03_L02_Q17
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.RR.2
Question:
Which function reflects sqrt(x) over the x-axis?
{
=A. g(x) \= -sqrt(x)#Correct. A negative outside the radical reflects outputs over the x-axis.
~B. g(x) \= sqrt(-x)#This is a different transformation. Reflection over the x-axis requires a negative sign outside the radical because it changes the output values.
~C. g(x) \= sqrt(x) - 1#This is a different transformation. Reflection over the x-axis requires a negative sign outside the radical because it changes the output values.
~D. g(x) \= sqrt(x - 1)#This is a different transformation. Reflection over the x-axis requires a negative sign outside the radical because it changes the output values.
}


